                      <item>
                       <widget class="QLabel" name="other_mods_explanation_text">
                        <property name="text">
                         <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;To ensure any other mods you wish to use play nicely with each other, put them in separate folders in the &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;other_mods&lt;/span&gt; directory and choose which ones you want to apply together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For example, if you have a mod which changes Link's tunic color, you can create a new folder in the &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;other_mods&lt;/span&gt; directory named &amp;quot;Other Tunic Color&amp;quot; and put the &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;romfs&lt;/span&gt; folder of that mod into the new folder. Then refresh the mod list and it should appear below. We do not currently support mods that modify any files in the &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;exefs&lt;/span&gt; folder.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
                        </property>
